  "notes": "No images were opened or downloaded, so nothing was judged by eye; every URL was only checked with a header request and returned 200 as an image. Photos were found in the page HTML and in the Elementor style sheets the pages load (the four home page slides, and the page header backgrounds). Where WordPress served a sized copy (for example diver-2-1024x768.jpg) the full-size original without the size suffix is recorded, and it loads. Logo is the site header logo, logo.jpg. It is a JPG, not SVG, PNG or WebP; the only PNG candidate is the site icon android-chrome-512x512-1.png (the page share image), which was not recorded as the logo because it was not confirmed to be the same mark. heroImage cruises.jpg is the widest of the home page slides (the 1024 by 610 sized copy) and is unseen, so a person should confirm it; dolphin-1.jpg is the site's first slide. Left out of hero and gallery: the 673 by 600 page header PNGs (about.png, ourboat.png, the-lena-1.png, divers.png, Dive-cruises.png, dophin-1.png), which are named like page graphics and could not be checked for printed text; dophin-1.png and ourboat.png are listed only at the end of the cruise trips for the importer to measure. Also left out: map.png (a map picture), the Quality Tourism Australia accreditation badge (quality-tourism-acredited-business3.jpg and its thumb), and the site icons. The site has no gallery page and no photo credits. Trip photo lists follow the page each photo sits on: the home, About and Our Boat pages share one photo set for Scenic Cruises, Twilight Cruise and Private Functions, so those three trips list the same pool in a different order, and Dive Charters uses the Dive page photos. Dive-cruises.png from the Dive page was left out of that list by the limit of 10. The Lena page is about a dive site, not a trip, so its photo Diving-on-the-Lena.jpg is in the gallery and its other photos (the-lena-1.jpg) were not listed. No videos: the site has no YouTube or Vimeo embeds or links. Its only social link is Facebook, which was not opened. No bot check, captcha or block was met on any page."
